1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:01,840
Mark 4

2
00:00:01,840 --> 00:00:05,740
Again he began to teach beside the sea,

3
00:00:06,120 --> 00:00:08,480
and a very large crowd gathered about him,

4
00:00:08,700 --> 00:00:11,600
so that he got into a boat and sat in it on the sea,

5
00:00:11,920 --> 00:00:14,760
and the whole crowd was beside the sea on the land.

6
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:17,880
And he was teaching them many things in parables,

7
00:00:18,140 --> 00:00:19,940
and in his teaching he said to them,

8
00:00:20,700 --> 00:00:21,120
Listen!

9
00:00:21,980 --> 00:00:23,760
A sower went out to sow,

10
00:00:24,220 --> 00:00:27,220
and as he sowed some seed fell along the path,

11
00:00:27,220 --> 00:00:29,380
and the birds came and devoured it.

12
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,180
Other seed fell on rocky ground where it did not have much soil,

13
00:00:33,480 --> 00:00:36,640
and immediately it sprang up since it had no depth of soil.

14
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:39,200
And when the sun rose it was scorched,

15
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:41,820
and since it had no root it withered away.

16
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:44,420
Other seed fell among thorns,

17
00:00:44,680 --> 00:00:46,500
and the thorns grew up and choked it,

18
00:00:46,760 --> 00:00:48,140
and it yielded no grain.

19
00:00:48,740 --> 00:00:51,920
And other seeds fell into good soil and produced grain,

20
00:00:52,380 --> 00:00:55,060
growing up and increasing and yielding thirtyfold,

21
00:00:55,060 --> 00:00:57,860
and sixtyfold, and a hundredfold.

22
00:00:58,320 --> 00:00:59,380
And he said,

23
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:03,280
He who has ears to hear, let him hear.

24
00:01:05,120 --> 00:01:06,580
And when he was alone,

25
00:01:06,840 --> 00:01:09,880
those around him with the twelve asked him about the parables,

26
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:11,380
and he said to them,

27
00:01:12,120 --> 00:01:14,780
To you has been given the secret of the kingdom of God,

28
00:01:15,160 --> 00:01:17,560
but for those outside everything is in parables,

29
00:01:18,080 --> 00:01:20,420
so that they may indeed see but not perceive,

30
00:01:20,800 --> 00:01:22,920
and may indeed hear but not understand,

31
00:01:23,560 --> 00:01:25,800
lest they should turn and be forgiven.

32
00:01:26,320 --> 00:01:27,700
And he said to them,

33
00:01:28,440 --> 00:01:29,800
Do you not understand this parable,

34
00:01:29,800 --> 00:01:32,880
how then will you understand all the parables?

35
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:35,380
The sower sows the word,

36
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:37,820
and these are the ones along the path,

37
00:01:38,080 --> 00:01:39,000
where the word is sown.

38
00:01:39,300 --> 00:01:41,380
When they hear, Satan immediately comes

39
00:01:41,380 --> 00:01:43,460
and takes away the word that is sown in them.

40
00:01:44,080 --> 00:01:46,300
And these are the ones sown on rocky ground,

41
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:48,180
the ones who when they hear the word

42
00:01:48,180 --> 00:01:50,160
immediately receive it with joy,

43
00:01:50,680 --> 00:01:52,920
and they have no root in themselves,

44
00:01:52,920 --> 00:01:54,660
but endure for a while.

45
00:01:55,260 --> 00:01:57,940
Then when tribulation or persecution arises

46
00:01:57,940 --> 00:01:58,960
on account of the word,

47
00:01:59,500 --> 00:01:59,780
immediately,

48
00:01:59,800 --> 00:02:01,040
they fall away.

49
00:02:01,800 --> 00:02:04,260
And others are the ones sown among thorns.

50
00:02:04,740 --> 00:02:06,160
They are those who hear the word,

51
00:02:06,500 --> 00:02:07,940
but the cares of the world

52
00:02:07,940 --> 00:02:09,520
and the deceitfulness of riches

53
00:02:09,520 --> 00:02:11,860
and the desires for other things

54
00:02:11,860 --> 00:02:13,520
enter in and choke the word,

55
00:02:13,760 --> 00:02:15,220
and it proves unfruitful.

56
00:02:15,720 --> 00:02:18,240
But those that were sown on the good soil

57
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:19,920
are the ones who hear the word

58
00:02:19,920 --> 00:02:21,940
and accept it and bear fruit

59
00:02:21,940 --> 00:02:24,180
thirtyfold and sixtyfold

60
00:02:24,180 --> 00:02:25,540
and a hundredfold.

61
00:02:25,940 --> 00:02:27,320
And he said to them,

62
00:02:27,700 --> 00:02:29,280
Is a lamp brought in

63
00:02:29,280 --> 00:02:30,820
to be put under a basket

64
00:02:30,820 --> 00:02:31,900
or under a bed

65
00:02:31,900 --> 00:02:33,200
and not on a stand?

66
00:02:33,980 --> 00:02:35,340
For nothing is hidden

67
00:02:35,340 --> 00:02:36,860
except to be made manifest,

68
00:02:37,220 --> 00:02:38,560
nor is anything secret

69
00:02:38,560 --> 00:02:39,680
except to come to light.

70
00:02:40,580 --> 00:02:42,560
If anyone has ears to hear,

71
00:02:42,880 --> 00:02:43,900
let him hear.

72
00:02:44,620 --> 00:02:45,620
And he said to them,

73
00:02:46,280 --> 00:02:48,160
Pay attention to what you hear.

74
00:02:48,540 --> 00:02:49,860
With the measure you use,

75
00:02:50,060 --> 00:02:51,360
it will be measured to you,

76
00:02:51,360 --> 00:02:53,460
and still more will be added to you.

77
00:02:54,340 --> 00:02:55,700
For to the one who has,

78
00:02:55,800 --> 00:02:56,540
more will be given.

79
00:02:57,100 --> 00:02:58,600
And from the one who has not,

80
00:02:58,600 --> 00:03:01,360
even what he has will be taken away.

81
00:03:02,020 --> 00:03:02,800
And he said,

82
00:03:03,580 --> 00:03:04,700
The kingdom of God

83
00:03:04,700 --> 00:03:07,380
is as if a man should scatter seed on the ground.

84
00:03:07,840 --> 00:03:10,100
He sleeps and rises night and day,

85
00:03:10,280 --> 00:03:11,900
and the seed sprouts and grows.

86
00:03:12,280 --> 00:03:13,460
He knows not how.

87
00:03:14,080 --> 00:03:16,080
The earth produces by itself,

88
00:03:16,580 --> 00:03:18,100
first the blade, then the ear,

89
00:03:18,380 --> 00:03:19,720
then the full grain in the ear.

90
00:03:20,220 --> 00:03:21,920
But when the grain is ripe,

91
00:03:22,180 --> 00:03:23,800
at once he puts in the sickle,

92
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:25,800
because the harvest has come.

93
00:03:26,520 --> 00:03:27,380
And he said,

94
00:03:27,720 --> 00:03:28,380
With what seed?

95
00:03:28,600 --> 00:03:30,360
What can we compare the kingdom of God?

96
00:03:30,740 --> 00:03:32,880
Or what parable shall we use for it?

97
00:03:33,720 --> 00:03:35,940
It is like a grain of mustard seed,

98
00:03:36,240 --> 00:03:37,680
which when sown on the ground

99
00:03:37,680 --> 00:03:40,220
is the smallest of all the seeds on earth.

100
00:03:40,780 --> 00:03:41,860
Yet when it is sown,

101
00:03:41,940 --> 00:03:43,580
it grows up and becomes larger

102
00:03:43,580 --> 00:03:44,940
than all the garden plants,

103
00:03:45,100 --> 00:03:46,740
and puts out large branches,

104
00:03:47,280 --> 00:03:48,660
so that the birds of the air

105
00:03:48,660 --> 00:03:50,420
can make nests in its shade.

106
00:03:51,140 --> 00:03:52,420
With many such parables

107
00:03:52,420 --> 00:03:53,680
he spoke the word to them

108
00:03:53,680 --> 00:03:55,160
as they were able to hear it.

109
00:03:55,640 --> 00:03:57,760
He did not speak to them without a parable,

110
00:03:57,760 --> 00:03:59,900
but privately to his own disciples

111
00:03:59,900 --> 00:04:01,440
he explained everything.

112
00:04:02,240 --> 00:04:04,140
On that day when evening had come,

113
00:04:04,320 --> 00:04:05,220
he said to them,

114
00:04:05,980 --> 00:04:08,040
Let us go across to the other side.

115
00:04:08,700 --> 00:04:09,700
And leaving the crowd,

116
00:04:09,880 --> 00:04:11,500
they took him with them in the boat,

117
00:04:11,700 --> 00:04:12,620
just as he was.

118
00:04:13,160 --> 00:04:14,560
And other boats were with him.

119
00:04:15,080 --> 00:04:16,880
And a great windstorm arose,

120
00:04:17,220 --> 00:04:19,100
and the waves were breaking into the boat,

121
00:04:19,180 --> 00:04:20,800
so that the boat was already filling.

122
00:04:21,360 --> 00:04:22,720
But he was in the stern,

123
00:04:22,860 --> 00:04:23,920
asleep on the cushion.

124
00:04:24,420 --> 00:04:26,100
And they woke him and said to him,

125
00:04:26,740 --> 00:04:27,140
Teacher,

126
00:04:27,140 --> 00:04:29,100
do you not care that we are perishing?

127
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:31,840
And he awoke and rebuked the wind,

128
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:32,980
and said to the sea,

129
00:04:33,720 --> 00:04:36,200
Peace, be still.

130
00:04:37,380 --> 00:04:38,960
And the wind ceased,

131
00:04:39,280 --> 00:04:40,640
and there was a great calm.

132
00:04:41,160 --> 00:04:41,940
He said to them,

133
00:04:42,700 --> 00:04:44,520
Why are you so afraid?

134
00:04:45,460 --> 00:04:47,340
Have you still no faith?

135
00:04:48,220 --> 00:04:50,220
And they were filled with great fear,

136
00:04:50,360 --> 00:04:51,460
and said to one another,

137
00:04:52,140 --> 00:04:53,740
Who then is this,

138
00:04:54,600 --> 00:04:55,740
that even the wind

139
00:04:55,740 --> 00:04:57,120
and the sea

140
00:04:57,140 --> 00:04:58,100
may obey him?

141
00:04:58,100 --> 00:05:28,080
Thank you.

